\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If a finitely generated group H is quasi-isometric to a finitely generated virtually polycyclic group P, must H itself be virtually polycyclic?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If a finitely generated group H is quasi-isometric to a finitely generated virtually polycyclic group P, must H itself be virtually polycyclic?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://www.math.utah.edu/~bestvina/eprints/questions-updated.pdf}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/quasi-isometric-recognition-of-virtually-polycyclic-groups-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

